# geo engine lives in maps-realestate — this is a machine-local link created by
# scripts/link-geo.js (npm run link:geo). Never commit it: the path differs per
# machine. NOTE: no trailing slash — a symlink is a file to git, not a directory.
src/geo

# The geo engine's SPEC is owned by the same project, so the pure-geo tests are
# links too (see GEO_ONLY_TESTS in scripts/link-geo.js). Gitignored for the same
# reason as src/geo: the relative target is machine-specific. `postinstall` and
# the deploy both run link-geo.js, so a fresh checkout gets them back. The five
# integration tests that import ./src/store/db stay REAL files (the atom's own
# store) and are guarded against drift by link-geo.js instead.
tests/bbox-prune.test.ts
tests/dedupe-suspects.test.ts
tests/dedupe.test.ts
tests/details-extract.test.ts
tests/geocode-guard.test.ts
tests/geo-trust-order.test.ts
tests/landmark-tiers.test.ts
tests/offlineMap.test.ts
tests/place-identity.test.ts
tests/resolve-offline.test.ts
tests/serp-capture.test.ts
tests/street-census.test.ts
tests/tile-coverage.test.ts
tests/type-normalize.test.ts

# Runtime pid of a restarted TUI — written by the deploy (maps-realestate's
# scripts/deploy_map.sh) on the machine running it, never a source artifact.
data/tui.pid
